      // shoot_range_m of the van; while it moves faster than moving_mps their rounds are turned off their line by up to moving_aim_error_deg (rival_crew.json's gun.aim_error_deg is the standing one). The car stops (brakes, the handbrake once it nearly
      // stands) and the crew gets out and fights on foot as a Rival crew when the van is slower than stop_speed_mps within stop_within_m, when its driver is dead (it rolls; stop_seconds at most), or when it made no 1 m/s for stalled_seconds while it wants on.
      // Before that, a car wedged (under 1 m/s with the van beyond follow_m) for unstick_after_seconds backs out for reverse_seconds and drives on, at most max_unsticks times in a row (the count is forgotten after 3 s at 3 m/s).
      // REMOUNT: a crew on foot whose van is more than remount_m from its nearest living member and pulling away (the gap grows faster than pull_mps, smoothed, for remount_confirm_seconds) walks back to its car over the navigation mesh and gets in (the
      // seats as when it spawned) when the car is not wrecked, no player sits in it and its driver lives; remount_seconds to do it, then it stays on foot and tries again after remount_retry_seconds. A wrecked or taken car: they stay on foot.
      // follow_m: the gap it keeps (it slows below the van's speed when closer, speeds up by catch_up_gain per metre of gap beyond it, at most max_speed_mps = 23.33, 84 km/h: 1.4 times the loaded Cartel van's 60 km/h, or far_speed_mps = 33, 120 km/h while the gap is more than far_m = 100 (the rubber band: a car left far behind catches up; 84 km/h close, 120 km/h far); an NPC's input only,
